===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sweh₂d-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|swete}}, from {{inh|en|ang|swēte||sweet}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*swōtī}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*swōtuz||sweet}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*swéh₂dus||sweet}}.

Cognate and synonymous with {{cog|sco|sweit|t=sweet}}, {{cog|frr|sweete|t=sweet}}, {{cog|stq|swäit|t=sweet}}, {{cog|fy|swiet|t=sweet}}, {{cog|nl|zoet|t=sweet}}, {{cog|nds-de|sööt|t=sweet}}, {{cog|de|süß|t=sweet}}, {{cog|da|sød|t=sweet}}, {{cog|sv|söt|t=sweet}}, {{cog|no|søt|t=sweet}}, {{cog|is|sætur|t=sweet}}, {{cog|la|suāvis}}, {{cog|sa|स्वादु|tr=svādú}}, {{cog|grc|ἡδύς}}. {{doublet|en|suave}}.

