|passage=a voice '''sweet''', tremulous, but powerful}}
# Of a [[pleasing]] [[disposition]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''sweet''' child}}
#: {{ux|en|You're so '''sweet'''!}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=Mitchy Collins; Samantha Derosa; Christian Medice|authorlabel=no|title={{w|Broken (Lovelytheband song)|Broken}}|album=w:Finding It Hard to Smile|date=13 April 2017|artist=w:Lovelytheband|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AToJekZdLIE|text=There's something tragic, but almost pure / Think I could love you, but I'm not sure / There's something wholesome, there's something '''sweet''' / Tucked in your eyes that I'd love to meet}}
# Of a [[helpful]] [[disposition]].
#: {{ux|en|It was '''sweet''' of him to help out.}}
# {{lb|en|mineralogy}} Free from [[excessive]] [[unwanted]] [[substance]]s like [[acid]] or [[sulphur]].
#: {{ux|en|'''sweet''' gas}}
#: {{ux|en|'''sweet''' soil}}
#: {{ux|en|'''sweet''' crude oil}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} Very [[pleasing]]; [[agreeable]].
#: {{ux|en|The new Lexus was a '''sweet''' birthday gift.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1932|year_published=1965|author=w:Delos W. Lovelace| title={{w|King Kong (1933 film)|King Kong}}| page=1| passage=Her crew knew that deep in her heart beat engines fit and able to push her blunt old nose ahead at a '''sweet''' fourteen knots, come Hell or high water.}}
#* '''14 November 2014''', Steven Haliday, ''Scotland 1-0 Republic of Ireland: Maloney the hero''
#*: GORDON Strachan enjoyed the '''sweetest''' of his 16 matches in charge of Scotland so far as his team enhanced their prospects of Euro 2016 qualification with a crucial and deserved victory over Republic of Ireland.
# {{lb|en|Australian|slang}} Doing well; in a [[good]] or [[happy]] [[position]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=John Hoskison|title=Inside: One Man's Experience of Prison|passage="Visit in two days though," said Tommo. "Hang in there mate, got a [[joey]] coming, we'll be '''sweet''' then."}}
# {{anchor|be_sweet_on}}{{lb|en|informal|followed by {{m|en|on}}}} [[romantic|Romantically]] [[fixate]]d; [[enamor]]ed with; [[fond]] of.
#: {{ux|en|The attraction was mutual and instant; they were '''sweet''' on one another from first sight.}}
# {{cap|fresh}}; not [[salt]] or [[brackish]].
#: {{ux|en|'''sweet''' water}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1627|author=w:Francis Bacon|chapter=Sylva Sylvarum: or A Natural History|title=The Works of Francis Bacon|page=66|year_published=1826 
|passage=The white of an egg, or blood mingled with salt water, doth gather the saltness and maketh the water '''sweeter'''; this may be by adhesion.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1821|author=Robert Thomas|title=The modern practice of physic| page=713| passage=Nothing has been found so effectual for preserving water '''sweet''' at sea, during long voyages, as charring the insides of the casks well before they are filled.}}
# {{lb|en|of soil|UK|dated}} {{cap|alkaline}}.
# {{senseid|en|pleasing to the eye}} {{cap|pleasing}} to the [[eye]]; [[beautiful]]; [[mild]] and [[attractive]]; [[fair]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''sweet''' face}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''sweet''' colour or complexion}}
#* '''1667''', {{w|John Milton}}, ''{{w|Paradise lost}} ([[s:Page:Paradise lost by Milton, John.djvu/284|source]])'', {{w|Samuel Simmons}}, page 278:
